# Subagent worktrees. Each holds a complete checkout with its own node_modules, so without
# this rule `git status` in the main checkout is dirty while a parallel task runs, and the
# `git add -A` of another review would take them.
.claude/worktrees/

# The Vercel CLI writes here when it links the project, and its project file holds the
# `projectId` and the `orgId`: they belong to the account and not to the repo, so a commit
# of them would tie the clone of anyone else to this Vercel project.
.vercel/

# The state of a run of the implementation protocol: logs, approvals, evidence, handoffs.
# The PR and the issue are the durable record. See .agents/protocols/implementation-protocol.md.
.agent-runs/

# What a mutation run writes: the sandbox of Stryker and its report. `pnpm mutation`.
.stryker-tmp/
reports/
